  "title": "Chapter 22: Parliament of India",
  "order": 23,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qrbwyss",
      "content": "The Parliament of India is the supreme legislative body of the country. It represents the will of the people and makes laws for the nation. The Indian Parliament follows a bicameral system consisting of two houses: the Lok Sabha (House of the People) and the Rajya Sabha (Council of States), along with the President of India."
    },
