      "id": "e1of5j7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Parliament of India comprises two houses: the Lok Sabha (House of the People) and the Rajya Sabha (Council of States).",
        "Parliamentary operations proceed through designated Sessions of Parliament and specific steps in the Legislative Process.",
        "Parliamentary functions are divided into Legislative Powers, Financial Powers, Executive Control, and Judicial Powers.",
        "A Joint Sitting of Parliament is utilized to resolve legislative deadlocks between both houses."
      ],
      "id": "8olp402"
    },
