    {
      "id": "fdlk9go",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Joint Sitting of Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ipckhvy",
      "content": "A joint sitting of both Houses may be called by the President when there is a deadlock between Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha over a bill. It is presided over by the Speaker of Lok Sabha."
    },
    {
      "id": "ggajak8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Powers and Functions of Parliament"
    },
    {
      "id": "rgpr9ty",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Legislative Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "21vp4yo",
      "content": "• Makes laws for the country"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ox9knn1",
      "content": "• Amends the Constitution"
    },
    {
      "id": "0lfzhpj",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Financial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "twri7nx",
      "content": "• Approves the Union Budget"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jp69hpr",
      "content": "• Controls public expenditure"
    },
    {
      "id": "f58m14w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Executive Control"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kww1es4",
      "content": "• Council of Ministers responsible to Lok Sabha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pr2w726",
      "content": "• Parliament can remove government through no-confidence motion"
    },
    {
      "id": "43lklkb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Judicial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional Articles Related to Parliament and its core structure are frequently asked in competitive exams.",
        "Distinguish carefully between the powers and composition of Lok Sabha (House of the People) and Rajya Sabha (Council of States).",
        "Questions often focus on the Types of Bills in Parliament and the procedural rules surrounding a Joint Sitting of Parliament."
      ],
      "id": "7dtv1rv"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "sea4rxk",
      "content": "• Impeachment of President"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9v7447v",
      "content": "• Removal of judges of Supreme Court and High Courts"
    },
    {
      "id": "dvsor3o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "df3b1nj",
      "content": "• Parliament consists of President, Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3yd6xe1",
      "content": "• Lok Sabha maximum strength 552."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "phuvnfu",
      "content": "• Rajya Sabha maximum strength 250."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z6n35fc",
      "content": "• Money Bill introduced only in Lok Sabha."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ipzjjln",
      "content": "• Joint sitting presided by Speaker of Lok Sabha."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
